  "notes": "A compound of {援|えん} (aid) and {護|ご} (protect). Originally a military term for providing covering fire or protective support, now commonly used figuratively in everyday and business contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {援護|えんご}する — to provide support, to back up\n- {援護|えんご}{射撃|しゃげき} — covering fire\n- {援護|えんご}を{求|もと}める — to seek support\n- {戦傷病者|せんしょうびょうしゃ}{戦没者|せんぼつしゃ}{遺族|いぞく}{等|とう}{援護|えんご}{法|ほう} — war veterans' support law\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {支援|しえん} — support, assistance (broader, more general)\n- {応援|おうえん} — cheering, support (encouraging someone)\n- {援助|えんじょ} — aid, assistance (material or financial help)\n- {庇護|ひご} — protection, patronage (sheltering from harm)",
